Spec consequence: a var() referencing an unset custom property with no fallback makes the declaration invalid
at computed-value time; the affected property computes to its initial value (for background: transparent).
So every .glass/.card/button/.phone/.desktop/.sheet/.msg/.banner/.inset/... background is transparent;
borders, box-shadows and backdrop-filter still render -> flat outline/ghost look, not the intended material.
